+# Inert declared Yarn selector core
+
+`DeclaredYarnClosure` is a build-logic utility, **not an installed ordinary root
+policy**. No root hook is wired by this addition. It uses only Kotlin/JDK APIs;
+normal builds do not acquire a Python runtime or a second maintained parser.
+
+## Restricted contract
+
+The caller must establish **stable-owned inputs**: the selected input tree is
+exclusively owned, root/ancestor identities are stable, and there are no concurrent
+writers, link/reparse substitutions or imported untrusted filesystem objects. The current
+NIO reader is **non-atomic**. Its pre/post path checks and `NOFOLLOW_LINKS` detect
+existing links and observed changes, not every race. A substituted FIFO can block
+an open despite the byte cap. Windows reparse/junction, macOS, concurrent-writer
+and FIFO behavior are not certified by Linux model evidence. An eventual adapter
+must establish a reviewed input/host contract; this documentation is not such an
+implemented gate.
+
+The registry-only profile checks required stored bytes first, all declared root
+normal/dev/optional seeds and literal workspace manifests, exact reachable Yarn
+selectors, bounded cycles/traces and canonical registry URL/SHA512 **syntax**.
+Unsupported aliases, Git and other protocols/policies refuse explicitly. The
+actual JS alias/Git policy, separate Wasm tooling, mandatory closure-before-restore,
+cold/warm/direct/bootstrap ordering and actual child arguments remain separate
+unresolved adoption requirements. An empty root map never skips workspaces.
+
+Syntactically valid wrong SRI, unsatisfied semver ranges or an omitted edge plus
+its omitted stanza are not independently detected. There is no fetched-byte,
+advisory/provenance, cache-trust, security, release or complete dependency-integrity
+claim. BUILD-007/#40 remains open; publishing and all independent readiness gates
+are unchanged.
+
+## Owned receipt snapshot
+
+`CheckedGraph.inputs` keeps the same read-only public `List<InputReceipt>` getter,
+but copies constructor inputs into a private JDK unmodifiable list. A Kotlin
+read-only type alone is not JVM immutability: exposing a multi-element `toList()`
+backing list permits removing or replacing receipts used by later rechecks. The
+copy also disconnects a writable constructor alias. Immutable receipt fields and
+fresh rechecks are retained; no filesystem atomicity or resolver trust is added.
+
+## Repository-owned tests
+
+`DeclaredYarnClosureModelTest` contains **32 synthetic JVM model methods**. Every
+lock and manifest is generated from authored Kotlin strings inside a fresh
+exclusive temp tree. No generated project/third-party package JSON, existing
+package lock, raw Yarn fixture, host cache, network input or private fixture path
+is included. The setup uses only the standard `java.io.tmpdir` parent, resolves
+its existing aliases before creating the test-owned tree and deletes only that
+tree without following links. No custom system property, test resource copy or
+new test dependency is required; the convention build already has JUnit4.13.2.
+
+The symlink method explicitly probes creation capability in its owned tree. If
+that one capability is unavailable it is **skipped**, not a host-safety success;
+its reader assertions are never caught or waived. Nonregular-input refusal is a
+separate method so it does not disappear when link creation is unavailable.
+Regular-reader identity/provider failures are failures, not blanket host skips.
+All method results must be inspected separately from compilation.
+
+The earlier private33-method/model compiler evidence remains unchanged. Twenty-nine
+synthetic method bodies are byte-preserved here; the combined filesystem method
+is split into two with repository-capability setup, one new receipt-snapshot
+regression is authored, and three external snapshot/raw-input methods are deliberately
+excluded. That evidence does not prove this
+new ordinary fixture setup ran. **At preparation, zero repository methods or
+Gradle tasks have executed.** Do not add32 to the historical33 as unique coverage.
+
+One owning convention compile/test request, once scheduled and externally bounded
+by the lead with the required 8 GiB reserve and serial local-build capacity:
+
+```sh
+JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-amd64 \
+./gradlew -p convention-plugins compileKotlin compileTestKotlin test \
+  --tests 'io.github.apdelrahman1911.nativecmpkit.buildlogic.DeclaredYarnClosureModelTest.existingLeafAndAncestorSymlinksAreRefused' \
+  --tests 'io.github.apdelrahman1911.nativecmpkit.buildlogic.DeclaredYarnClosureModelTest.existingNonregularStoredInputIsRefusedWithoutSymlinkCapability' \
+  --tests 'io.github.apdelrahman1911.nativecmpkit.buildlogic.DeclaredYarnClosureModelTest.checkedInputReceiptsAreAnUnmodifiableOwnedSnapshot' \
+  --offline --no-daemon --no-configuration-cache --no-build-cache --max-workers=1 --no-parallel \
+  '-Dorg.gradle.jvmargs=-Xmx1024m -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=384m -XX:ActiveProcessorCount=1 -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8' \
+  -Pkotlin.compiler.execution.strategy=in-process
+```
+
+This single request typechecks the inert utility and test setup, then selects only
+the two changed filesystem fixtures and one new receipt-snapshot regression. It
+does not replay the 29 applicable accepted synthetic bodies or existing publication
+tests. Inspect the exact three fresh XML methods and every failure/skip; a symlink
+capability skip is not verification. A missing offline cache input must remain a
+real refusal, not trigger an automatic network/install or validation bypass.
+
+Compilation and these synthetic methods do not run library/sample/native tests,
+install Yarn, enforce ordinary dependency closure, establish convention dependency
+trust, verify other hosts, clear security requirements or authorize publication.
+The lead must preserve source/results hashes and owned process/output cleanup.
